scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:1395:draftly-rule-courts-coa-HCC-21-20-JUDGMENT-4.pdf-1,courts-coa-HCC-21-20-JUDGMENT-4.pdf,,COA,,"A witness's credibility is not affected by trivial contradictions in their testimony, especially when they are consistent on the main points of the incident.","I hold that this trivial contradiction does not affect the credibility of this witness. On the other hand, he will remember what is important, which should have always been in his memory, because that incident would not fade from his memory.",SRC029-s165,none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
