scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:865:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1988-6-1,commonlii-LKSC-1988-6,(1988) 1 Sri LR 78,LKSC,1988,"An agreement to sell is not a disposal of the house within the meaning of s. 10 of the Ceiling of Housing Property Law. Since the plaintiff had not disposed of the house before 13th January 1974, the premises vested in the Commissioner of National Housing under s. 11","(1) An agreement to sell is not a disposal of the house within the meaning of s. 10 of the Ceiling of Housing Property Law. Since the plaintiff had not disposed of the house before 13th January 1974, the premises vested in the Commissioner of National Housing under s. 11(1) of the Law. No vesting order is necessary. The vesting is by operation of law. (2) A tenant who has been let into possession is estopped from denying his landlord's title or from asserting that another person has a better title than his landlord (s. 116 of the Evidence Ordinance). But this doctrine has no",,none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
