scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\cache\courts-sc-sc_appeal_60_2004.pdf.json:8:   "supporting_quote": "However, in MMBL Teas (Pvt) Ltd. v. British Ceylon Produce Export (Pvt) Ltd. [S.C. Case No. SC/CHC/35/2008, S.C.M. 17.12.2021] Aluwihare, PC, J., (at page 17) was of the view that failure to challenge evidence by cross examination by itself may not be sufficient to hold that a particular fact had been proved within the meaning of Section 3 of the Evidence Ordinance. It might, however, be a factor to be taken into account in accepting such evidence.",
